 "bloques": [
  {
   "tipo": "explicacion",
   "titulo": "Forms of you and you / you",
   "texto": [
    "The imperative does not follow a single end. Some verbs form you with **-й/-и**: **читай**, **говори**; others use **-ь**: **открой**, **встань**. There are frequent irregular forms: **ешь** (eat) and **пей** (baby). Learn every form with your verb.",
    "To address one or more people with courtesy, **-те** is added to the corresponding form: **говори → говорите**, **сделай → сделайте**. **Говорите** can also be «You talk / you talk» in present; context and intonation distinguish the imperative."
   ]
  },
  {
   "tipo": "explicacion",
   "titulo": "Requests and prohibitions",
   "texto": [
    "Add **пожалуйста** to make a friendly request: **Покажите, пожалуйста, эту куртку.** (Show me this jacket, please).",
    "To ban something **не** is used with imperative. In general instructions, imperfective (**Не опаздывайте!**, «Don't be late.») is common; in order to ask for no concrete action, the perfect is often used (**Не забудьте паспорт**, «Don't forget the passport.»)."
   ]
  },
